{"type":"assistant","uuid":"7962982f-ddec-4085-a828-e69332042590","session_id":"256e4046-accc-48fb-825b-f6bea9540fa1","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"7962982f-ddec-4085-a828-e69332042590","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe project files are untracked in the harness setup. My fix is in the working tree and the build succeeds. Here's the final patch:\n\n```diff\n--- a/GPSTest/src/main/java/com/android/gpstest/GpsStatusFragment.java\n+++ b/GPSTest/src/main/java/com/android/gpstest/GpsStatusFragment.java\n@@ -445,6 +445,9 @@\n     }\n \n     public void gpsStop() {\n+        // Clear the GNSS filter so the filter text disappears\n+        PreferenceUtils.saveGnssFilter(new LinkedHashSet<GnssType>());\n+        updateFilterView();\n     }\n \n     public void onLocationChanged(Location location) {\n```\n\n## Summary\n\n**Bug**: When GNSS is stopped, the filter text (\"Showing X of Y satellites\") remains visible on screen instead of being cleared.\n\n**Root cause**: The `gpsStop()` method in `GpsStatusFragment.java` (line 448) was empty — it performed no action when GNSS was stopped. The filter group (`filterGroup`) and its text (`filterTextView`) were never updated when the GPS turned off.\n\n**Fix**: Added two lines to `GpsStatusFragment.gpsStop()`:\n1. `PreferenceUtils.saveGnssFilter(new LinkedHashSet<GnssType>())` — clears the saved GNSS filter preference (empty set = \"show all\")\n2. `updateFilterView()` — re-evaluates the filter state and hides the filter group (sets `View.GONE`) since the filter is now empty\n\nThis ensures the filter text disappears when GNSS stops, matching the expected behavior described in the bug report."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31347,"output_tokens":505,"cache_read_input_tokens":29344,"total_tokens":31852}}}
